  "generated_text": "To determine if $f(x) = \\frac{5^x - 1}{5^x + 1}$ is even, odd, or neither, we need to evaluate $f(-x)$ and compare it to $f(x)$.\n\n1. Calculate $f(-x)$:\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{5^{-x} - 1}{5^{-x} + 1}\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify $f(-x)$:\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{5^x} - 1}{\\frac{1}{5^x} + 1}\n   \\]\n\n3. Compare $f(-x)$ to $f(x)$:\n   \\[\n   f(-x) = \\frac{1 - 5^x}{1 + 5^x} = -\\frac{5^x - 1}{5^x + 1} = -f(x)\n   \\]\n\n   Since $f(-x) = -f(x)$, the function $f(x)$ is an odd function.\n\nConclusion:\n$f(x)$ is an odd function. Therefore, the answer is $\\boxed{\\text{odd}}$.",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[odd, '\\\\text{odd}']",
    "gold_answer": "We have that\n\\begin{align*}\nf(-x) &= \\frac{5^{-x} - 1}{5^{-x} + 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 - 5^x}{1 + 5^x} \\\\\n&= -\\frac{5^x - 1}{5^x + 1} \\\\\n&= -f(x),\n\\end{align*}so $f(x)$ is an $\\boxed{\\text{odd}}$ function.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
